WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:06.819
Toni wrote in, Tony says, Hey David, which
drugs do you think should be legalized or

00:00:06.819 --> 00:00:08.120
decriminalized?

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:13.530
So number one, it's good that you're making
the distinction between legalized and decriminalized

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:18.350
because legalization and decriminalization,
uh, are, are very different things.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:23.640
And also it's important to distinguish between
trafficking and personal use.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:24.640
Okay.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.740
So let's go in order.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:33.030
All drug use and drug possession for personal
amounts should be decriminalized, period.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:34.970
Uh, legalization.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:38.200
Absolutely for marijuana and for other drugs.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.920
I'm open to discussion you.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:40.920
I believe it's Denver.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:45.020
That's testing, uh, legalizing, uh, mushrooms
as an example.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:52.079
I have less of a fixed opinion about the legalization
of some drugs.

00:00:52.079 --> 00:00:59.250
I've not seen good reasons to legalize recreational
cocaine or heroin for example.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:05.680
I'm very clear that possessing cocaine or
heroin for personal use should not be a crime.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:09.630
Using cocaine or heroin should not be a crime.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:15.570
Uh, but the recreational legalization of cocaine
and heroin, I just, I've not seen a good argument

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:18.510
for that and I'm willing to have my mind change.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:23.810
Now this gets us to a really important element
of this debate that a lot of people miss.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:30.340
A lot of people seem not to understand that
when you talk about legalization or decriminalization

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:37.720
of any drug, uh, you're not talking about
it being legal to be trafficking in those

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:38.720
drugs.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.600
10 pounds of marijuana or a kilo of Coke or
whatever.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:48.740
Whether you decriminalize or legalize, that
is likely still going to be criminal.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:53.970
And when you think about it, alcohol is legal
recreationally.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:55.880
Cigarettes are legal recreationally.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:02:00.720
It is still against the law to traffic and
alcohol or cigarettes without doing it, you

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.490
know, on the record as a business in the way
that the, the guidelines say that you should,

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:05.760
you can have that debate.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.439
And I'm, I'm glad to have it.

00:02:07.439 --> 00:02:11.260
Uh, but it's important to understand and I
think that there are a lot of bad faith actors

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.489
on the anti decriminalization.

00:02:13.489 --> 00:02:19.019
Anti legalization tends to be the political
right in the United States who either are

00:02:19.019 --> 00:02:25.029
misunderstanding or they are deliberately
conflating the decriminalization or legalization

00:02:25.029 --> 00:02:30.930
of the trafficking of drugs versus legalization
and decriminalization of amounts for personal

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:31.930
use.

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:33.419
And these are very, very different conversations.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:41.379
So my question to you today is, what is the
strongest argument for recreational legalization

00:02:41.379 --> 00:02:44.060
of drugs like cocaine and heroin?

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:47.639
I am 110% on board with marijuana.

00:02:47.639 --> 00:02:55.620
Uh, I would sooner make cigarettes illegal
than say that marijuana should remain criminal

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.319
for use and possession.

00:02:57.319 --> 00:03:03.870
Uh, but I, I simply have not seen a good case
made for why there should be recreational,

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.609
illegal cocaine or heroin.

00:03:06.609 --> 00:03:10.620
But if you've got a good argument to make
along those lines, by all means get in touch

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:10.881
and then we can talk about it.

